    "body": "Hmm I could move the non-connected case into the dialog/fullscreen cases which would allow hidePopover() on a disconnected element to not throw an exception...\r\n@jakearchibald do you think that the following should throw an exception?\r\n```javascript\r\nconst div = document.createElement('div');\r\n// don't connect div to the document\r\ndiv.setAttribute('popover', 'auto');\r\ndiv.hidePopover();\r\n```",
